DTSTAMP:20261007T022859Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Morning intervals · threshold · 9.5 km
DESCRIPTION:• 2 km easy warm-up\n• 5 × 1 km at 3:45–3:50/km\, 90 s j
 og between\n• 2 km easy cool-down\n• Reps should feel hard but even. I
 f the last rep is more than 5 s slower than the first\, stop there\n\nWhy:
  Raises your threshold so marathon pace feels easier. Kept below 5k pace b
 ecause you raced two days ago.\n\nFuel: None during. Have carbs and protei
 n within an hour afterwards.\n\nHeart rate guide (estimated from your rece
 nt runs\, may be off):\n• 5:20–5:45/km: easy\, HR 125–150. Over 150 
 means slow down\n• 3:45–3:50/km: HR about 172–182\n\nhttps://joshuam
 orley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
