BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:akl-2026-10-18@joshuamorley.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T022859Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Half marathon · Test 2 · 21.1 km
DESCRIPTION:• Run it as a controlled training run\, not a race. Two weeks
  out is too close to race a half\n• First 16 km at 4:15/km\n• Last 5 k
 m easy to steady\, 4:45–5:15/km. Don't speed up\n• If HR goes past 170
  before 16 km\, ease off. That tells you something useful\, it isn't a fai
 lure\n• Note your average pace and HR over the first 16 km\, and whether
  you could have kept going\n\nWhy: The best guide to your race pace you'll
  get before race day\, without taking so much out of you that it hurts the
  marathon.\n\nFuel: Race-day routine: breakfast 3 h before\, a gel 10–15
  min before the start\, then gels at about km 6\, 11 and 17\, each with wa
 ter.\n\nHeart rate guide (estimated from your recent runs\, may be off):\n
 • 4:13–4:17/km: HR about 158–170\n• 4:45–5:15/km: steady\, HR ab
 out 140–158\n\nhttps://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
